        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: prevent operational notices from leaking to source chats",
        "body": "<details>\n<summary>Additional instructions</summary>\n\n**MUST:** Keep **Allow edits from maintainers** enabled for this PR so maintainers can help update the branch when needed.\n\n</details>\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users in external chats such as WhatsApp could see automatic runtime notices when model fallback, usage limits, compaction, backend failures, heartbeat checks, ACP status, plugin-binding failures, or tool/progress warnings happened.\n\nAI-assisted: yes, Codex helped update this branch and evidence.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds `messages.operationalReplies` so operators can control automatic operational notices separately from normal assistant replies. The policy supports `always`, `silent`, `once`, and `redirect`; `redirect` writes notices to an operator session through `redirectSessionKey`, and `sendPolicy: deny` still wins.\n\nThe policy is applied across direct dispatch, ACP delivery, ACP status projection, queued follow-ups, compaction notices, route-failure notices, heartbeat delivery, progress/status callbacks, plugin-binding notices, tool warnings, and block/final replies. Normal message-tool replies, authorized command replies, before-run block replies, and background ACP child suppression keep their existing behavior.\n\nRedirect-failure behavior uses the maintainer-selected fail-closed contract: if the configured operator redirect write fails, the source chat remains suppressed and the failure is logged instead of exposing operational details back to the source chat.\n\nA follow-up review found plain `isError` payloads were too broad to classify as operational notices. This branch now treats only explicit notice flags or internal notice metadata as operational, and it keeps normal error replies visible under `messages.operationalReplies`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can keep fallback, usage-limit, backend-error, compaction, heartbeat, status, ACP, follow-up, plugin-binding, and tool-warning notices out of external chats while still preserving logs or redirecting those notices to an operator-owned session. Existing configs keep current behavior because the default policy is `always`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `ac2c5870b063222097124a9720802eed711e74f8`\nCurrent base checked locally: `b0ebb81e89f5217397d409c996e2bbf914623a94` (`origin/main`)\n\nLatest validation after merging current `origin/main`:\n\n- `TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.tmp\" node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --check` - passed\n- `TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.tmp\" node --max-old-space-size=8192 --import tsx scripts/generate-plugin-sdk-api-baseline.ts --check` - passed\n- `TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.tmp\" node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.auto-reply-reply.config.ts src/auto-reply/reply/operational-reply-policy.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/dispatch-acp-delivery.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/dispatch-from-config.test.ts` - 3 files, 341 tests passed\n- `TMPDIR=\"$PWD/.tmp\" node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts src/infra/heartbeat-runner.clears-pending-final-delivery.test.ts` - 1 file, 8 tests passed\n- `git diff --cached --check` - passed before commit\n- `git diff --check` - passed before commit\n\nEarlier validation in this sweep:\n\n- Full focused auto-reply set passed before later base movement: 4 files, 505 tests passed.\n- A later full focused rerun hit local SQLite `disk I/O error` failures only in `followup-runner.test.ts`; the three other auto-reply files passed.\n- `codex review --base origin/main` found no high-confidence actionable regression in the changed operational-reply paths on the prior latest-base push; bundled autoreview refused the full branch diff because it was over its size limit.\n- Local Testbox/Crabbox warmup was blocked by `[crabbox] selected binary failed basic --version/--help sanity checks`, so focused local wrappers were used.\n\nNot run: full `pnpm test`, full `pnpm check`, full `pnpm build`, remote Testbox/Crabbox proof, or live WhatsApp delivery proof.\n",
